# Names only. Do not put real values in this file.
# OWNER_TOKEN must be at least 32 characters.
# GMAIL_API_BASE and GOOGLE_TOKEN_URL are optional. Leave them unset in production.
# NODE_ENV=production refuses any origin other than https://gmail.googleapis.com
# and https://oauth2.googleapis.com. Defaults are those two.
# GMAIL_PUSH_JWKS is optional and only for tests. NODE_ENV=production refuses it.
# Production verifies push tokens with Google's published keys.
# OWNER_TIMEZONE is an IANA name, such as America/New_York. It is required when
# MAIL_PROVIDER is not fake. A fake provider that omits it uses UTC and logs that
# at startup. A snooze or remind label dated today wakes at 06:00 in this zone.
# GMAIL_TIMEOUT_MS is optional. Default is 20000. A read that hits it is retried once.
# A write that hits it is not.
# MAIL_PROVIDER is fake, gmail, imap, or live. fake is the demo mailbox and is
# refused in production. gmail requires GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
# and can also store IMAP and Microsoft accounts. live turns on every real
# provider, and each one works only when its own config is set. Without a Google
# client, /connect/google says Google sign-in is not set up. An IMAP account is
# usable once it is connected. A Microsoft tool call says Microsoft sign-in is
# not set up until MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID is set.
# IMAP_ALLOW_PRIVATE_HOSTS=1 allows private and loopback hosts so tests and a
# local Dovecot can connect. Dev and tests only. NODE_ENV=production refuses
# to start if this name is set.
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID is the Entra application id. Set MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET
# only for the owner's own web app. Leave the secret unset for device-code
# sign-in on the shared public client. A secret without an id refuses to start.
# MICROSOFT_GRAPH_BASE, MICROSOFT_TOKEN_URL, MICROSOFT_AUTH_URL, and
# MICROSOFT_DEVICE_URL are optional. Leave them unset in production. Production
# accepts only https://graph.microsoft.com and https://login.microsoftonline.com.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET are required when MAIL_PROVIDER=gmail.
# OWNER_PASSPHRASE is the one sign-in passphrase. There is no second user.
# PUBLIC_URL is an https origin with no path. NODE_ENV=production refuses to
# start when it is missing. It is the issuer, the token audience, and Google's
# redirect host.
# OAUTH_REDIRECT_HOSTS is a comma-separated list of hosts that may receive an
# authorization code. The default is claude.ai, the host in
# https://claude.ai/api/mcp/auth_callback. Loopback is allowed only when
# NODE_ENV is not production. Add a host here to allow another client.
# GOOGLE_AUTH_URL is optional. Leave it unset in production. Production accepts
# only https://accounts.google.com. Tests may point it at a local fake.
# VERCEL=1 or TRUST_PROXY=1 trusts x-forwarded-host and x-forwarded-proto.
# Vercel sets VERCEL. Do not set a secret in either name.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENROUTER_API_KEY turns on summaries, triage, and
# drafts at /app. The key stays on the server. If both are set, Anthropic runs.
# SAMPLE_MODEL is the one model id sent to whichever of those is configured.
# When it is unset, Anthropic uses claude-haiku-5-5 and OpenRouter uses
# anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5. ANTHROPIC_API_BASE and OPENROUTER_API_BASE are
# optional. Production accepts only https://api.anthropic.com and
# https://openrouter.ai.

IMAP_ALLOW_PRIVATE_HOSTS=

OWNER_TOKEN=
ENCRYPTION_KEY=
MAIL_MODE=
MAIL_STORE=
MAIL_PROVIDER=
DATABASE_URL=
PORT=
HOST=

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_GRAPH_BASE=
MICROSOFT_TOKEN_URL=
MICROSOFT_AUTH_URL=
MICROSOFT_DEVICE_URL=
GMAIL_API_BASE=
GOOGLE_TOKEN_URL=
GMAIL_TIMEOUT_MS=
SYNC_DAYS=
